From 71945829df943e6c38cae638efc25bfbe8cfdf8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duck-brain <duck-brain@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:23:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] duck-brain P28: the tick journal never overwrites a run, and
 is out within 2 s

Alex, 08.11: a restart of robotd with the same --journal truncated a walk
of 18 057 ticks.
- A journal path that exists is never truncated: the new run goes to
  <stem>-<UTC start time>.<ext> beside it (-2, -3 if taken), and robotd
  logs the path it writes.
- The batch period drops from 180 s to 2 s: the journal lives in RAM
  (/run, /tmp) on the duck, where a batch costs nothing, and the 180 s was
  for the SD card. A relax (any kind: torque off), a change of the fall
  verdict and a change of the driving network write it out at once,
  after that tick's line.
A robotd that dies loses at most the last 2 s. A file in RAM is itself
lost at power-off, whatever the batches.
---
 robotd/src/journal.rs | 181 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 robotd/src/main.rs    |  20 ++++-
 2 files changed, 182 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

