+//! to RAM (`/run`, `/tmp`) and a batch costs nothing; it was 180 for the SD card — or when [`BUFFER`]
+//! fills, and at once on [`Journal::flush_now`] (a relax, a fall, a change of network), and at the
+//! end. What a robotd that dies loses is the last batch. A file in RAM is itself lost at power-off.
+//!
+//! **Never over an earlier run** (P28): a path that already exists is not truncated; the journal
+//! goes to `<stem>-<UTC start time>.<ext>` beside it instead ([`free_path`]).
 
 use std::io::Write;
 use std::path::Path;
@@ -34,29 +38,96 @@ pub const BUFFER: usize = 16 << 20;
